{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CIA Triad.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CIA Triad.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cia triad cia triad","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CIA Triad.md","fileName":"CIA Triad.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CIA Triad","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:39\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Security and Data Protection]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security and Data Protection","Information Confidentiality","Data Integrity","Information Availability","cloudcomputing_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CIA Triad.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CIA Triad.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cia triad cia triad","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CIA Triad.md","fileName":"CIA Triad.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CIA Triad","heading":"CIA Triad","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The CIA triad describes information security through [[Information Confidentiality|confidentiality]], [[Data Integrity|integrity]], and [[Information Availability|availability]]. Confidentiality limits disclosure, integrity protects correctness and intended use, and availability makes information or services accessible when needed.\n\nThe three properties expose different kinds of failure. A system can keep data secret while allowing unauthorized alteration, or can preserve correct data that users cannot reach in time, so a security requirement should address each property separately.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Security and Data Protection","Information Confidentiality","Data Integrity","Information Availability","cloudcomputing_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CIA Triad.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CIA Triad.md","sourceType":"markdown